{"nodes": [{"id": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite", "label": "ADR-0005 PostgreSQL as the database", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_postgresql16", "label": "PostgreSQL 16", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Free, no licence acceptance, small footprint, real row-level locking, xmin as a schema-free concurrency token, and advisory locks for distributed locking with no extra infrastructure. Decisive here: no Docker daemon, while PostgreSQL 16 was already installed and startable natively.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_xmin_token", "label": "xmin system column as concurrency token", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Mapped as Version with type xid; costs nothing in schema because pg_attribute.attnum = -2 makes Npgsql's migration generator emit no DDL. Postgres-specific: porting to SQL Server means a byte[] RowVersion with [Timestamp].", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_select_for_update", "label": "SELECT \u2026 FOR UPDATE row locking", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Standard SQL, and it ports to SQL Server as WITH (UPDLOCK, ROWLOCK).", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_sqlite_rejected", "label": "SQLite (rejected on capability)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Locking is file/database-level, not row-level \u2014 writers serialise across the whole database, so a pessimistic lock on one account is indistinguishable from a lock on every account. No SELECT FOR UPDATE, no meaningful deadlock scenario; a test proving pessimistic locking works would pass for the wrong reason.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_sqlserver_rejected", "label": "SQL Server (rejected on friction)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The close call, lost on friction rather than merit: large image, EULA acceptance, more memory than a lab container has, and no Docker daemon in this environment. Its rowversion token is the more familiar one to .NET developers, which ADR-0006 covers explicitly.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite", "target": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_postgresql16", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_postgresql16", "target": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_xmin_token", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_postgresql16", "target": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_select_for_update", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_postgresql16", "target": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_sqlite_rejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_postgresql16", "target": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_sqlserver_rejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite_xmin_token", "target": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_bankdbcontext", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite", "target": "adr_0012_postgres_advisory_locks", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0005_postgresql_over_sqlserver_sqlite", "target": "adr_0015_local_postgres_over_testcontainers", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0005-postgresql-over-sqlserver-sqlite.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}